{
  "_doc": "Look proof views (harness/bin/lookproof.mjs). Each view is a fresh game run at its size: it loads a stand-in scene (P0-009: street, landmarks, areas), puts the debug camera at a fixed pose (hud_play keeps the chase camera and the HUD), lets 1 s of sim pass, then holds the sim (hold at 0 pauses at once) so every run shoots the same moment. The scenes are seeded and static. P1-026: views with \"group\": \"city\" are for the streamed city (the game's default scene, full pilot tiles): each teleports the player (the streaming ring follows it), puts the debug camera at a fixed pose and holds the sim. lookproof --set takes the views of one group: --group <name>, else \"city\" for a set whose name starts with city_ and otherwise the views with no group (the stand-in look views). Group \"city_systems\" are ablation views for the per system table (citybase.mjs).",
